# Witness: a declaration among the arguments alone takes the first position: in `g(int: b 2)` it goes to the
# int input a, which admits no declaration Structure; the call is refused, answer 4
# Norm: the book #declaration-selection (its table), #admission; the plan #two-kinds-of-receivers-plan item 1; R65-R68, R71, R76.
# Slice «selection of the declaration by the call» (plan #two-kinds-of-receivers-plan).
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
)

fn: g (int: a; int: b) int
    return: b

sub: main () (
    int: k 0
)
    @: shared node[0]
    shared\Observed\seen := g(int: b 2)
main()
